  <iati-identifier>GB-CHC-285776-COL179</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-285776" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving protection and capacity of human rights defenders and organisations in Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to improve the protection and capacity of Human Rights Defenders (HRDs) and HRD organisations who are working for the rights of victims of armed conflict in five departments of Colombia. These departments have been chosen due to their high levels of human rights violations and where the work of human rights defenders and civil society organizations are facing serious obstacles and pressures, including life-threatening situations. 
 
This project will combine both practical support and emergency assistance to HRDs, capacity development activities for HRDs and HRD organisations, and a strong component of national and international advocacy to tackle the root causes of injustice facing HRDs and victims of the armed conflict.
 
This project is 81% funded by the European Commission&apos;s European Instrument for Democracy and Human Rights budget line and will be implemented in Colombia by SNPS (Caritas Colombia) and ABColombia (international advocacy element). Both are established partners of CAFOD. SCIAF will be a collaborating partner. We will also be working with other Caritas agencies (Caritas Norway, Trocaire, Caritas Switzerland and CIDSE in awareness-raising/advocacy activities) and with CAFOD&#x2019;s Governance Team and CIDSE around the issue of civil society space and the Busan process.  

The total budget for the project is Euro 1,140,879 and the project will be completed over 36 months. The remaining contributions come from CAFOD CGF, CAFOD CDF and SCIAF funds.</narrative>
  </description>
